            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0320" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.4061 Motion Pictures/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-30T12:00:00+00:00">October 30,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 30—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>929. Reference my despatches numbers 2250 and 2266 of October 18 and 29.<anchor
                        n="38" xml:id="d194-f1"/> As a result of the Embassy’s representations just
                    prior to the Cabinet meeting yesterday morning, the Foreign Office has now
                    informed me that the Cabinet definitely decided not to issue the projected
                    decree law for regulation of the moving picture industry.</p>
                <p>This means that the matter can only arise again if projects for legislation on
                    this subject come before Parliament when it meets.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Straus</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
